","notes":"Walk to 124 North Wayne Street and browse the genre-spanning record bins during the shop’s posted Wednesday–Saturday window.","short_summary":"A compact downtown record stop with both new and vintage titles.","evidence_claim":"Wax Galaxy Records at 124 North Wayne Street carries hundreds of new and vintage vinyl titles across multiple genres.","source_url":"https://www.visitmilledgeville.org/listings/wax-galaxy-records/42154/","source_title":"Wax Galaxy Records","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The current listing states Wednesday–Saturday, 10 a.m.–6 p.m.; confirm hours directly before going.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"georgias-old-capitol-building","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Georgia's Old Capitol Building","title":"Study the Gothic Public Architecture","subtitle":"East Greene Street corridor","notes":"Follow East Greene Street to Statehouse Square and examine the Old Capitol’s granite steps, pointed arches, and towers.","short_summary":"A former statehouse whose exterior makes Georgia political history tangible.","evidence_claim":"Georgia’s Old Capitol Building is at 201 East Greene Street and features granite steps, pointed arches and large towers dating to its 1807 Gothic design.","source_url":"https://www.visitmilledgeville.org/listings/georgias-old-capitol-building/41823/","source_title":"Georgia's Old Capitol Building","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Exterior viewing may be possible from Statehouse Square; verify public interior access with Georgia Military College.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"georgias-old-governors-mansion","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Georgia's Old Governor's Mansion","title":"Tour a Restored 1839 Residence","subtitle":"South Clarke Street corridor","notes":"Turn onto South Clarke Street and time your arrival for an hourly tour of the mansion’s restored 19th-century interior.","short_summary":"An interpreted house museum connecting architecture, politics and antebellum society.","evidence_claim":"The mansion at 120 South Clarke Street was completed in 1839, restored to its 1851 appearance and operates as a historic house museum.","source_url":"https://www.visitmilledgeville.org/listings/georgias-old-governors-mansion/1/","source_title":"Georgia's Old Governor's Mansion","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Tours are listed Tuesday–Saturday, 10 a.m.–4 p.m., and Sunday, 2–4 p.m., beginning each hour; closures apply.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"sallie-ellis-davis-house","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Sallie Ellis Davis House","title":"Enter a Recreated Classroom","subtitle":"South Clarke Street corridor","notes":"Continue south on Clarke Street to explore the recreated classroom and learn how Davis supported students at Eddy High School.","short_summary":"A preserved educator’s home interpreting Black education and community care.","evidence_claim":"The Sallie Ellis Davis House at 301 South Clarke Street includes a recreated classroom and preserves the educator’s work with Eddy High School students.","source_url":"https://www.visitmilledgeville.org/blog/post/reasons-to-visit-the-sallie-ellis-davis-house/","source_title":"The Legacy of Sallie Ellis Davis: African American Educator in Milledgeville","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":"2026-01-21","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Tours are offered Wednesdays and Fridays, selected weekends, and by arrangement; call 478-445-5889 to confirm.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"bone-cemetery","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Bone Cemetery","title":"Locate the Eddy Tour’s Cemetery Stop","subtitle":"Liberty Street corridor at Franklin Street","notes":"Use the entrance map at Liberty and Franklin Streets to find documented burials, and keep your visit quiet and respectful.","short_summary":"A reflective Eddy Neighborhood stop tied to Black civic and military history.","evidence_claim":"Bone Cemetery is at Liberty and Franklin Streets and includes documented burials of physician B. J. Simmons and three Buffalo Soldiers from the 9th Cavalry.","source_url":"https://www.visitmilledgeville.org/blog/post/the-eddy-neighborhood/","source_title":"Exploring The Eddy Neighborhood: African American History in Milledgeville, Georgia","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":"2026-01-21","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the cemetery map at the entrance, remain on established paths and observe respectful daylight visiting practices.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
